00:00:00.090 --> 00:00:04.110
First of all, most people don't realize
how long it takes to learn a language.

00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:07.080
Hi there, this is Steve
Kaufmann from Palm Springs.

00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:11.010
Uh, today I'm going to talk
about problems, problems people

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:12.060
have in language learning.

00:00:12.570 --> 00:00:18.030
Remember if you enjoy these videos,
please subscribe and they click

00:00:18.030 --> 00:00:19.530
on the bell for notifications.

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:23.490
And if you follow me on a podcast
service, please leave a review.

00:00:25.020 --> 00:00:26.760
First of all, why am I
talking about problems?

00:00:27.210 --> 00:00:31.950
Because I, my whole filming set up
has, is giving me nothing but problems.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:37.890
Last video, I had this reflection on
those prints that I have in behind me.

00:00:37.890 --> 00:00:41.820
The time before that I filmed in front of
the curtain, which didn't look very nice.

00:00:42.090 --> 00:00:45.930
I've ordered some hanging sort of
backdrops, but I haven't figured

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.190
out how to pin them up yet.

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:50.640
And then it'll at least looked
like some fake bookshelves.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.445
Uh, Or I got another one
that's fake wooden planks.

00:00:56.015 --> 00:00:59.825
Uh, but then I've ordered little skinny
bars so that my wife can sow a little

00:00:59.825 --> 00:01:01.235
thing and we can hang it up there.

00:01:01.235 --> 00:01:03.725
And then the lighting is all
messed up and it's not working.

00:01:03.725 --> 00:01:07.025
And my filmic pro is giving me problems.

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:10.325
So I just got fed up with
it all, all my problems.

00:01:10.895 --> 00:01:14.789
And I said, I'm just going to go
out in the garden and do it and

00:01:14.789 --> 00:01:17.880
I'm going to talk about problems,
language learning problems.

00:01:18.179 --> 00:01:21.090
What are the main problems that
I see amongst language learners?

00:01:21.119 --> 00:01:23.759
I'm going to try to center
myself here again, problems.

00:01:24.090 --> 00:01:28.050
First of all, most people don't realize
how long it takes to learn a language.

00:01:28.360 --> 00:01:30.030
So people get frustrated.

00:01:30.420 --> 00:01:34.470
They get particularly frustrated when
they get to that first level where

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:37.950
all of a sudden they know a bunch of
words and they realize just how little

00:01:37.950 --> 00:01:42.479
they know of the whole language and
people get frustrated and they have

00:01:42.479 --> 00:01:43.860
the sense that they're not progressing.

00:01:44.310 --> 00:01:47.400
And maybe they think that everyone
else is learning and I'm not learning.

00:01:47.789 --> 00:01:52.950
And I think that's where it's so
important to realize A that it's a long

00:01:52.950 --> 00:01:57.479
process and B that you have to find
a way of doing it that is enjoyable.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:00.990
So I don't worry about the fact
that I've been at Arabic and Persian

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:04.830
for a long time and there are other
people who learn faster than me.

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:06.149
I'm enjoying it.

00:02:06.149 --> 00:02:11.519
I was listening to my Egyptian Arabic
mini stories that have been now rerecorded

00:02:11.519 --> 00:02:17.595
by Adel of Alexandria and I was going
through the texts again and it's fun.

00:02:17.625 --> 00:02:18.405
I enjoy it.

00:02:18.435 --> 00:02:21.255
And I know that trickle,
trickle, trickle I'm improving.

00:02:21.285 --> 00:02:25.035
So the first thing I find is a lot
of people don't have the patience.

00:02:25.635 --> 00:02:30.975
Second problem is a lot of people,
and I find this myself too, you know?

00:02:30.975 --> 00:02:34.455
So I'm doing the mini stories,
Adel's mini stories and I've gone

00:02:34.455 --> 00:02:35.955
through two or three of them.

00:02:36.615 --> 00:02:39.915
Uh, it's not like instantly I've
done something like I've built

00:02:39.915 --> 00:02:41.685
something or made something happen.

00:02:42.015 --> 00:02:46.710
I'm just doing this and I have to remind
myself that it is actually slowly,

00:02:46.710 --> 00:02:48.660
the language is trickling into me.

00:02:48.840 --> 00:02:52.350
So don't worry about doing something
else, continue doing what you're doing

00:02:52.830 --> 00:02:54.960
and do as much of it as you want.

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.790
If you do 15 minutes, that's good.

00:02:56.790 --> 00:02:58.080
If you do a half an hour is good.

00:02:58.380 --> 00:03:02.775
You don't have to say I have to do
two hours a day, every little helps.

00:03:02.805 --> 00:03:06.495
So I think that's an important part
of, you know, making sure that the

00:03:06.495 --> 00:03:09.705
time you spend with the language, you
don't begrudge yourself that time.

00:03:09.885 --> 00:03:11.085
You're happy doing it.

00:03:11.265 --> 00:03:15.105
And if it's 10 minutes, 20 minutes, half
an hour or two hours, it's all good.

00:03:15.885 --> 00:03:18.795
Third problem people have with
language learning is they don't

00:03:18.795 --> 00:03:22.755
like to make mistakes and therefore
they are intimidated, intimidated.

00:03:22.755 --> 00:03:26.535
So, you know, I always stress input,
but of course we all want to speak.

00:03:27.345 --> 00:03:30.554
All, most people want to speak,
and we want to speak with as few

00:03:30.554 --> 00:03:32.744
mistakes as possible of course.

00:03:32.954 --> 00:03:36.045
However, I like speaking with mistakes...

00:03:36.734 --> 00:03:40.515
not that I don't want to improve,
but I know that if I speak

00:03:40.515 --> 00:03:41.834
with mistakes, I'm speaking.

00:03:42.765 --> 00:03:46.035
And I had a conversation
this morning in German.

00:03:46.035 --> 00:03:47.265
I made so many mistakes.

00:03:47.265 --> 00:03:50.415
It's been so long since I spoke
German and I speak it so seldom.

00:03:51.899 --> 00:03:54.089
In that conversation I
was getting feedback.

00:03:54.089 --> 00:03:55.140
I was getting input.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.220
We were communicating.

00:03:56.369 --> 00:03:59.549
If I were to do that more,
my German would improve.

00:03:59.700 --> 00:04:04.230
Not only because I'm speaking, but
also because I'm getting input back.

00:04:04.649 --> 00:04:07.140
And so mistakes are a good thing.

00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:08.609
Mistakes are not a bad thing.

00:04:08.880 --> 00:04:13.230
Unfortunately, too often, uh, the
traditional language teaching,

00:04:13.649 --> 00:04:18.240
you know, instructional methods
teaches us to be afraid of mistakes.

00:04:19.050 --> 00:04:20.760
Well, there's nothing wrong with mistakes.

00:04:20.760 --> 00:04:24.360
It's not like we're building a bridge
and we might design it wrong and

00:04:24.360 --> 00:04:25.590
the bridge is going to collapse.

00:04:25.590 --> 00:04:26.430
It's not like that.

00:04:26.670 --> 00:04:30.450
If we're communicating, we're
already achieving the main goal

00:04:30.930 --> 00:04:34.950
and if we want to improve, but
we're not afraid to make mistakes.

00:04:35.340 --> 00:04:37.620
That's the ideal attitude to have.

00:04:37.980 --> 00:04:40.530
So, you know, you know you're
speaking with mistakes.

00:04:40.590 --> 00:04:42.420
It doesn't bother you
to speak with mistakes.

00:04:42.540 --> 00:04:45.960
The other person isn't judging
you, but at the same time, You're

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:47.190
listening to what they're saying.

00:04:47.190 --> 00:04:49.020
You're listening to how
the language is used.

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:51.840
You're continuing your input activities.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:55.470
And so you therefore
are gradually improving.

00:04:55.950 --> 00:05:00.360
So I think those would be three major
problems that language learners face.

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:03.720
In other words, they don't
realize that it's a long process.

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.960
Number two, they sometimes
begrudge themselves the time

00:05:06.960 --> 00:05:07.920
they're spending with it.

00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:10.680
Three they're afraid of making mistakes.

00:05:10.830 --> 00:05:15.210
And I guess the fourth one, which kind
of summarizes all those three is they're

00:05:15.210 --> 00:05:17.880
not finding ways to enjoy the process.

00:05:18.420 --> 00:05:20.670
They shouldn't be measuring
how well they're doing.

00:05:20.849 --> 00:05:23.630
They should be saying, wow,
I'm enjoying what I'm doing.

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:28.920
And so whatever, however you do that
because you choose content that you

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:31.080
like, or you activities that you like.

00:05:31.140 --> 00:05:36.090
If the emphasis is placed on enjoying
the process, you will gradually improve.

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:38.370
So just a brief chat.

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.820
And I realized too, and it makes
me happy that many people use my

00:05:41.820 --> 00:05:43.650
videos to work on their English.

00:05:43.680 --> 00:05:46.560
So I try to speak as clearly as possible.

00:05:46.920 --> 00:05:47.340
Okay.

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:48.210
Thanks for listening.

00:05:48.360 --> 00:05:48.900
Bye for now.

